<title>ITALY: Italian Jan car registrations rose 4.38 pct yr/yr.</title>
<headline>Italian Jan car registrations rose 4.38 pct yr/yr.</headline>
<dateline>ROME 1997-02-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>Italian new car registrations rose 4.38 percent to 207,000 units in January, compared with 198,308 in January 1996, the Ministry of Transport said.  </p>
<p>Total Italian new car registrations in the 1996 Jan-Dec period were 1,736,047, up 0.25 percent on the same period in 1995, the ministry said.</p>
<p>		 Jan 97	Mkt shre     Jan 96   Mkt shre</p>
<p>	   registrations </p>
<p>Fiat	     93,030     44.95	 92,022	46.40</p>
<p>Volkswagen     25,190     12.17	 24,900	12.55</p>
<p>General Motors 18,910	9.13	 17,490	 8.82</p>
<p>Ford	     17,220	8.32	 17,882	 9.02</p>
<p>PSA Peugeot    12,960	6.26	 12,361	 6.24</p>
<p>Renault	  12,280	5.93	 11,128	 5.61</p>
<p>BMW		9,230	 4.46	 6,651	  3.35</p>
<p>Mercedes	 3,520	 1.70	 2,816	  1.42</p>
<p>Nissan	   3,880	 1.87	 3,684	  1.86</p>
<p>Volvo	    2,080	 1.00	 1,740	  0.88</p>
<p>NOTE - Fiat comprises Fiat, Alfa Romeo, Lancia Autobianchi, and Fiat-Innocenti. Volkswagen comprises VW, Audi, Skoda and Seat. General Motors comprises Opel and Saab. PSA-Peugeot comprises Peugeot and Citroen. BMW comprises BMW and Rover.</p>
<p>-- Milan bureau +392 66129502</p>
